msgstr "For a TOML-like file where only free-form comment lines should be checked:"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:168
msgid "This will ignore tables and assignments while still checking plain text lines that do not match those patterns."
msgstr "This will ignore tables and assignments while still checking plain text lines that do not match those patterns."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:171
msgid "Built-in languages still win"
msgstr "Built-in languages still win"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:173
msgid "SLS schemas are a fallback only. If a file extension already has a built-in tree-sitter extractor, lang-check keeps using the built-in extractor for that extension."
msgstr "SLS schemas are a fallback only. If a file extension already has a built-in tree-sitter extractor, lang-check keeps using the built-in extractor for that extension."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:177
msgid "That means:"
msgstr "That means:"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:179
msgid "a custom `.rst` schema will not replace the built-in reStructuredText extractor,"
msgstr "a custom `.rst` schema will not replace the built-in reStructuredText extractor,"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:181
msgid "a custom `.md` schema will not replace Markdown,"
msgstr "a custom `.md` schema will not replace Markdown,"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:182
msgid "schemas are primarily for new extensions that do not already have first-class support."
msgstr "schemas are primarily for new extensions that do not already have first-class support."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:185
msgid "When to use extension aliases instead"
msgstr "When to use extension aliases instead"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:187
msgid "If the new format is truly the same as an existing built-in format, a simple extension alias in `.languagecheck.yaml` is usually better:"
msgstr "If the new format is truly the same as an existing built-in format, a simple extension alias in `.languagecheck.yaml` is usually better:"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:197
msgid "That reuses the target language's full tree-sitter extractor instead of the regex-based SLS fallback."
msgstr "That reuses the target language's full tree-sitter extractor instead of the regex-based SLS fallback."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:200
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr "Limitations"

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:202
msgid "SLS extraction is regex-based, not AST-aware."
msgstr "SLS extraction is regex-based, not AST-aware."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:203
msgid "Matching is line-oriented; nested syntax is not understood."
msgstr "Matching is line-oriented; nested syntax is not understood."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:204
msgid "Block skipping depends entirely on your `start`/`end` patterns."
msgstr "Block skipping depends entirely on your `start`/`end` patterns."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:205
msgid "If a format needs structural parsing, use the plugin workflow instead."
msgstr "If a format needs structural parsing, use the plugin workflow instead."

#: ../../guide-config-language.md:207
msgid "For a dedicated tree-sitter-based language integration, see [guide-plugin-language.md](guide-plugin-language.md)."
msgstr "For a dedicated tree-sitter-based language integration, see [guide-plugin-language.md](guide-plugin-language.md)."
